{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122201","id":4233384722,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc78VFMS","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122201","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122201.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122201.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122201","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122201/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122201/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122201/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b96d75b165ad12574087222b0c9eba1ef32b73a2","number":122201,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix: Inspector Should Not Collapse On Resource Save","user":{"login":"theraot","id":1212509,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTI1MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1212509?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot","html_url":"https://github.com/theraot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theraot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #122174\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nWhy was the inspector collapsing when the nested resource was saved? It wasn't, not technically. It was being rebuilt by `notify_property_list_changed`.\r\n\r\nWe can imagine a solution where we store what was folder or unfolder and unfold again. There is a simpler approach: Do not call `notify_property_list_changed`.\r\n\r\nSo, that's it, problem solved, right? Kind of. The resource is saved to a file, the inspector does not collapse, everything works, except we do not see changes reflected in the inspector. What changes? We should see resource file name.\r\n\r\nThus, we need a mechanism to update the inspector without rebuilding it. Turns out there is one, kind of. While testing with `notify_property_list_changed` removed I noticed that saving (Ctrl+S) would update the inspector correctly without folding or rebuilding it. Of course, I do not want to trigger a global save. So I needed to figure out how it did update the inspector. It took some experimentation to piece it together (I did try with `queue_redraw`, `emit_changed`...), what works is calling `update_property`, the problem is that I need to call `update_property` recursively and there isn't a reliable mechanism to do that (without doing other things). So I added one.\r\n\r\nI do not know if the approach is welcome: what I added is a new `update_properties_recursive` virtual method and implementation. At the end I figured I'd post it and let it be reviewed.\r\n\r\n| Before  | After |\r\n| ------------- | ------------- |\r\n|  <img width=\"368\" height=\"624\" alt=\"before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/55ae1352-dcfc-451f-8781-5f7b9649f403\" /> | <img width=\"368\" height=\"624\" alt=\"after\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b408cbbb-395a-4a21-93ae-477b43597f65\" /> |\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"